-# =============================================================================
-# RICH TEXT — FORM FIELD (Trix Editor)
-# =============================================================================
-#
-# Renders a Trix rich text editor for the given attribute.
-#
-# ─── HOW IT WORKS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-#
-# Trix is a web component: the <trix-editor> custom element. It connects to
-# a hidden <input> via the `input` attribute (matching the input's ID).
-# When the user types, Trix updates the hidden input's value with HTML.
-# On form submit, Rails receives the HTML string in the normal params hash.
-#
-# The hidden input is rendered by SimpleForm as a regular :hidden field.
-# We generate a unique ID for it so <trix-editor input="..."> can find it.
-#
-# ─── NO MODEL CHANGES NEEDED ────────────────────────────────────────────────
-#
-# This does NOT use ActionText's `has_rich_text`. The HTML is stored in a
-# plain :text column, same as before. Trix is used purely as a frontend
-# editor — the backend sees a regular string attribute.
-#
-# =============================================================================

- input_id = "trix_#{attribute}_#{form.object.class.model_name.param_key}_#{form.object.object_id}"

.mb-3
  - unless input_options[:label] == false
    %label.form-label{for: input_id}
      = input_options.fetch(:label, field_label)
  = form.hidden_field attribute, id: input_id
  %trix-editor.trix-content.form-control{input: input_id, class: input_options[:class]}
